// Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded sin(pi x) of F16
//
// x splits into x1 + x2: x1 keeps the top 11 bits of the F16 encoding, x2 the sign, the exponent and the low 5
// mantissa bits. Then sin(pi x) = sin(pi x1) cos(pi x2) + cos(pi x1) sin(pi x2), with the four factors F32 values
// from tables tuned so that this one F32 evaluation rounds correctly to F16 everywhere but one input, handled
// explicitly. Integers (every |x| >= 2^10) give +-0 with the sign of x. Round to nearest only.
//
// Also home to what sin_pi, cos_pi and tan_pi share: the cos(pi x1) and cos(pi x2) tables, the sin(pi x2) table
// that tan_pi uses too, and the NaN they return.
//
// Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binary16/sinpi/sinpif16.c via RazorForge's B16Sinpi.rf.
// Copyright (c) 2025 Paul Zimmermann
// MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module Standard::Core

